/-!
# Which reading of the VRF spec's Draft 35 the GP v0.8.1 path follows

GP v0.8.1 cites the Bandersnatch VRF-AD specification, Draft 35 (davxy/bandersnatch-vrf-spec
commit 181aba2), for all of Appendix G. In two places the draft's prose and its own test vectors
(Appendix C, generated by ark-vrf 0.5.0) disagree:

* **$Z_{\text{pad}}$.** App. A.2 instantiates hash_to_curve with "expand_message_xmd with SHA-512
  (section 5.3.1)" of RFC 9380, whose step 4 is
  $Z_{\text{pad}} = \text{I2OSP}(0, \mathit{s\_in\_bytes})$, 128 octets for SHA-512. The vectors need
  48 zero octets (Draft 36, commit fcf7012, later documents the 48 as a deliberate deviation). The
  three fixed points of §4 and §5 (blinding base $B$, accumulator base $S$, padding point $\square$)
  are stated to be hash_to_curve of their names, so under the prose reading they are derived with
  the 128-octet $Z_{\text{pad}}$, not taken from the coordinates the draft prints (which are the
  48-octet derivation).
* **Ring transcript label.** §5: "Begin with empty transcript and "ring-proof" label." The ring
  vectors verify only with the suite id `Bandersnatch-SHA512-ELL2-v1` as the label.

`Reading.prose` follows the prose and is the default of the v0.8.1 path (a project decision).
`Reading.vectors` follows the vectors and is what every published vector of the v0.8.1 path checks.
**No published vectors follow the prose reading**: it has no external oracle and is tested only
for self-consistency (`cryptotest`; see `docs/jamcrypto.md`). The v0.8.0 path has no reading: it
stays as validated against the 0.8.0 data.
-/

namespace JamCrypto

/-- The reading of the VRF spec's Draft 35 that the GP v0.8.1 path follows where its prose and its
    vectors disagree. -/
inductive Reading where
  /-- The cited spec's prose (the default). -/
  | prose
  /-- The spec's own test vectors. -/
  | vectors
  deriving DecidableEq, Repr, Inhabited

end JamCrypto
